1
00:00:00,950 --> 00:00:04,530
<i>The more time you spend with someone, 
the more you invariably learn about them.</i>

2
00:00:06,870 --> 00:00:09,640
<i>Her soul is in the early teens at most.</i>

3
00:00:10,240 --> 00:00:14,990
<i>Most of her knowledge's from the internet,
with very little first-hand experience.</i>

4
00:00:15,380 --> 00:00:17,580
<i>She's usually stupidly 
bright and cheerful,</i>

5
00:00:19,490 --> 00:00:20,250
<i>but at times,</i>

6
00:00:20,890 --> 00:00:23,340
<i>she has a look of total resignation 
on her face.</i>

7
00:00:24,730 --> 00:00:27,980
<i>Perhaps her previous life wasn't one 
she could look back fondly upon.</i>

8
00:00:28,590 --> 00:00:29,430
<i>Still...</i>

9
00:00:29,430 --> 00:00:32,180
Aqua, Ruby, dinner's ready.

10
00:00:32,710 --> 00:00:33,820
Coming!

11
00:00:36,010 --> 00:00:38,270
<i>Now that we've been reincarnated,</i>

12
00:00:38,840 --> 00:00:42,410
<i>as long as we're both living our best 
lives now, none of that matters.</i>

13
00:00:44,020 --> 00:00:47,360
m 0 0 l 0 102 32 102 b 3 75 3 32 32 0

14
00:00:44,020 --> 00:00:47,360
OSHI NO KO

15
00:00:44,020 --> 00:00:47,360
m 0 0 l 0 102 32 102 b 3 75 3 32 32 0

16
00:02:14,430 --> 00:02:16,870
The curry here is great!

17
00:02:17,240 --> 00:02:21,480
Check this out! The marrow-less bones 
can be used as straws!

18
00:02:22,500 --> 00:02:24,870
You can even drink your lassi with them!

19
00:02:28,030 --> 00:02:28,910
Wow!

20
00:02:28,910 --> 00:02:30,420
It's true! This is great!

21
00:02:30,420 --> 00:02:31,050
Right?

22
00:02:31,690 --> 00:02:33,420
Where should we go next?

23
00:02:33,420 --> 00:02:35,820
Everyone here is expecting to drink.

24
00:02:35,820 --> 00:02:40,150
Hmm, places nearby 
where we could drink in peace?

25
00:02:40,150 --> 00:02:40,890
How about Pater?

26
00:02:41,210 --> 00:02:43,580
Oh, I like it.

27
00:02:43,580 --> 00:02:47,750
A friend of mine runs that bar. 
I'll shoot them a LINE message.

28
00:02:48,930 --> 00:02:49,820
Aqua Hoshino

29
00:02:50,220 --> 00:02:51,950
Excuse me a second.

30
00:02:51,950 --> 00:02:53,240
Hey. What's up?

31
00:02:53,560 --> 00:02:54,990
Where are you?

32
00:02:54,990 --> 00:02:58,210
You haven't checked 
any of the items due today.

33
00:02:58,210 --> 00:03:01,740
<i>Uh, I'm out drinking 
with the marketing rep.</i>

34
00:03:02,020 --> 00:03:03,200
Marketing rep?

35
00:03:03,740 --> 00:03:08,860
<i>So they brought a bunch of "friends" 
who are models and actresses,</i>

36
00:03:08,860 --> 00:03:11,360
<i>and you're drinking at a hideaway bar?</i>

37
00:03:14,550 --> 00:03:18,300
I mean, networking is part of their job.

38
00:03:19,190 --> 00:03:22,160
And we always need good actors.

39
00:03:22,160 --> 00:03:23,270
<i>I'm not against it,</i>

40
00:03:24,030 --> 00:03:27,770
<i>but these things tend to be 
full of tough customers.</i>

41
00:03:28,240 --> 00:03:29,360
Don't get eaten alive.

42
00:03:33,200 --> 00:03:37,740
Of course. How many years do you 
think I've spent in this business?

43
00:03:43,770 --> 00:03:48,110
There's a lot about work that 
comes down to human feeling.

44
00:03:48,770 --> 00:03:51,670
Some things you can only see 
with alcohol in your system, too.

45
00:03:52,710 --> 00:03:57,930
This world runs on communication, 
and I'm a pro here.

46
00:03:59,840 --> 00:04:03,140
And pros never lose themselves in booze.

47
00:04:03,140 --> 00:04:06,390
Huh? My phone's gone!

48
00:04:06,390 --> 00:04:07,850
Where'd it go?

49
00:04:08,290 --> 00:04:11,920
Your phone's right here, Director Gotanda.

50
00:04:13,200 --> 00:04:13,900
Aqua-kun.

51
00:04:14,360 --> 00:04:15,710
Could you drag that thing home?

52
00:04:15,710 --> 00:04:17,910
Sure. I'll make sure the skunk gets home.

53
00:04:17,910 --> 00:04:19,110
Oh, hey, kid.

54
00:04:19,390 --> 00:04:21,430
Are you Aqua Hoshino-kun?

55
00:04:21,430 --> 00:04:25,230
I've heard all about you. 
You're the director's best student?

56
00:04:24,810 --> 00:04:26,280
Woohoo!

57
00:04:25,230 --> 00:04:27,570
No. I don't know this man.

58
00:04:27,980 --> 00:04:31,180
Now, now. It's raining 
outside, so join us.

59
00:04:31,180 --> 00:04:32,580
We'll call a taxi for you right away.

60
00:04:33,030 --> 00:04:34,590
Are you hungry?

61
00:04:34,590 --> 00:04:39,460
The Napolitan here is amazing. 
Eat that before you go, at least.

62
00:04:39,460 --> 00:04:40,840
No, thank you.

63
00:04:40,840 --> 00:04:43,020
You're always pestering the young ones.

64
00:04:43,020 --> 00:04:44,680
Give it a rest, Tendouji-san.

65
00:04:46,180 --> 00:04:48,840
Don't go giving me a bad name, now.

66
00:04:51,120 --> 00:04:53,860
Tendouji... Marina Tendouji?

67
00:04:53,860 --> 00:04:55,480
Why, yes.

68
00:05:03,470 --> 00:05:06,470
Did I give you my name?

69
00:05:07,580 --> 00:05:09,620
Here you are. Club soda.

70
00:05:09,620 --> 00:05:13,330
Let's go drinking as soon 
as you're old enough.

71
00:05:13,330 --> 00:05:17,230
But I guess you wouldn't want 
to go with an old lady like me.

72
00:05:17,230 --> 00:05:21,640
Don't worry. I'll bring 
some cute friends with me.

73
00:05:24,400 --> 00:05:26,010
You must love drinking.

74
00:05:26,340 --> 00:05:30,000
It's part of my job, in a way.

75
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:31,530
Is that really okay?

76
00:05:33,320 --> 00:05:36,140
Doesn't your family worry?

77
00:05:36,140 --> 00:05:39,170
Hey, I'm in my mid-fifties.

78
00:05:39,170 --> 00:05:44,710
And I've been doing this forever, 
so none of them worry about me.

79
00:05:46,660 --> 00:05:47,530
May I get to go to a B-Komachi concert

80
00:05:47,530 --> 00:05:48,540
May I get permission to go outside

81
00:05:48,540 --> 00:05:53,540
May Mom and Dad stay healthy
and never get sick

82
00:05:54,170 --> 00:05:56,040
You know somebody out there does.

83
00:05:56,600 --> 00:05:58,300
I suppose.

84
00:05:58,300 --> 00:06:00,380
I'm married.

85
00:06:00,700 --> 00:06:03,210
See, this is my family!

86
00:06:06,470 --> 00:06:09,520
<i>How is this even possible?</i>

87
00:06:11,100 --> 00:06:14,210
<i>Are there really parents like her?</i>

88
00:06:20,160 --> 00:06:23,450
<i>Sarina-chan...</i>

89
00:06:23,450 --> 00:06:28,910
Happy 54th, Mom!
Don't drink too much

90
00:06:24,350 --> 00:06:26,650
<i>Your life must've been a living hell.</i>

91
00:06:27,390 --> 00:06:28,910
When you have kids,

92
00:06:29,210 --> 00:06:32,620
all that matters 
is that they stay healthy.

93
00:06:33,500 --> 00:06:36,580
Mom... That's why Mom won't come...

94
00:06:36,580 --> 00:06:37,650
No.

95
00:06:37,650 --> 00:06:39,800
You're stuck on this bit again.

96
00:06:40,420 --> 00:06:42,230
Listen, in this scene,

97
00:06:42,230 --> 00:06:46,010
you're a child who starts to understand 
her mother who ran away from her.

98
00:06:46,350 --> 00:06:50,970
You admit that you're abnormal, 
and that your mother doesn't love you.

99
00:06:51,750 --> 00:06:56,780
You let her go, and you set yourself 
free in the process, too.

100
00:06:57,170 --> 00:07:01,120
You need to look relieved, not desperate.

101
00:07:00,360 --> 00:07:01,860
But that's all wrong.

102
00:07:03,560 --> 00:07:08,370
Admitting your mother doesn't love you? 
That can't be right.

103
00:07:09,110 --> 00:07:11,500
It's probably just a misunderstanding.

104
00:07:12,370 --> 00:07:16,370
The 15-Year Lie

105
00:07:12,820 --> 00:07:15,880
This makes no sense to me.

106
00:07:17,310 --> 00:07:19,130
I mean, after all...

107
00:07:19,980 --> 00:07:22,200
Deep down,

108
00:07:22,910 --> 00:07:25,520
parents always love their kids.

109
00:07:28,530 --> 00:07:29,390
<i>Ibaraki.</i>

110
00:07:29,870 --> 00:07:33,810
<i>Perform at a joint concert 
on an outdoor stage starting 6 PM.</i>

111
00:07:34,170 --> 00:07:35,710
<i>Get in the car at 9 PM.</i>

112
00:07:36,350 --> 00:07:38,100
<i>Back home at 11 PM.</i>

113
00:07:38,440 --> 00:07:40,120
<i>Go to school at 8:30 AM.</i>

114
00:07:40,590 --> 00:07:42,080
<i>Leave early at 10:30 AM.</i>

115
00:07:42,570 --> 00:07:48,530
Dig Deep!
Chase the Impawsible!!

116
00:07:42,570 --> 00:07:48,530
Dig Deep!
Chase the Impawsible!!

117
00:07:42,570 --> 00:07:47,520
Esperanto Lesson

118
00:07:42,570 --> 00:07:45,660
<i></i>Dig Deep! Chase the Impawsible!<i> 
prep meeting at 11:30 AM.</i>

119
00:07:46,220 --> 00:07:48,530
<i>Film a report at 12 PM.</i>

120
00:07:49,110 --> 00:07:51,650
<i>Get in the car at 3 PM, have lunch,</i>

121
00:07:51,650 --> 00:07:55,620
<i>approve interview text, 
and study for finals.</i>

122
00:07:55,620 --> 00:07:57,330
Yamada        Tanaka        Hoshino        Sasaki        Inoue

123
00:07:56,350 --> 00:07:57,330
<i>And at 4 PM,</i>

124
00:07:57,670 --> 00:08:01,650
<i>attend taping for a late-night 
variety show. Film three episodes.</i>

125
00:08:02,890 --> 00:08:05,880
<i>Practice choreo for a new song at 9:30 PM.</i>

126
00:08:06,430 --> 00:08:09,090
<i>And at the same time, 
discuss YouTube video ideas.</i>

127
00:08:09,780 --> 00:08:12,490
<i>One-on-one acting lessons at 11 PM.</i>

128
00:08:13,590 --> 00:08:16,050
<i>Go to bed at 3 AM.</i>

129
00:08:28,430 --> 00:08:32,620
Mom did all this without breaking a sweat.

130
00:08:33,220 --> 00:08:34,570
I need to do better.

131
00:08:35,330 --> 00:08:39,290
It's okay. I know I can do this.

132
00:08:42,380 --> 00:08:44,490
There's very little time 
before we start filming.

133
00:08:45,010 --> 00:08:49,260
I'd like you to pack Ruby-san's 
schedule with acting lessons.

134
00:08:49,610 --> 00:08:52,090
Ruby's doing all she can.

135
00:08:52,090 --> 00:08:56,200
Her schedule's already packed. 
She barely gets enough sleep.

136
00:08:56,200 --> 00:08:57,180
Even yesterday...

137
00:08:57,520 --> 00:09:00,300
Reduce the amount of work she takes on.

138
00:09:00,300 --> 00:09:02,850
Especially for the duration 
of filming and rehearsals.

139
00:09:03,650 --> 00:09:07,710
<i>The 15-Year Lie</i> will be 
a real test of acting chops.

140
00:09:07,710 --> 00:09:12,200
It might be cruel to say this about 
an actor as inexperienced as Ruby-san,

141
00:09:12,610 --> 00:09:16,360
but even I can see that 
she's lacking in ability.

142
00:09:18,700 --> 00:09:22,560
<i>Where does he get off saying that when he 
produced that </i>Sweet Today<i> live-action?</i>

143
00:09:24,190 --> 00:09:26,880
<i>But he's not wrong.</i>

144
00:09:27,260 --> 00:09:31,560
<i>Ruby doesn't have the skill 
to lead a cast that good.</i>

145
00:09:34,340 --> 00:09:36,050
Hoist the sails, mateys!

146
00:09:36,380 --> 00:09:38,810
Onward ho! To a brand new world!

147
00:09:41,800 --> 00:09:43,230
Not so fast!

148
00:09:43,600 --> 00:09:47,690
Only one of us can get her hands on 
that singular, legendary treasure!

149
00:09:47,690 --> 00:09:50,370
And I'll make sure it won't be you!

150
00:09:50,370 --> 00:09:52,290
Hah! Try me!

151
00:09:56,280 --> 00:09:57,240
<i>It's so hot!</i>

152
00:09:57,240 --> 00:09:58,200
<i>It's so hot!</i>

153
00:10:01,460 --> 00:10:04,710
When summer blazes hot, 
make sweat walk the plank...

154
00:10:04,660 --> 00:10:09,420
Body Wipes

155
00:10:04,660 --> 00:10:09,420
Soap Scented

156
00:10:04,660 --> 00:10:09,420
Spectaclean Body Wipes

157
00:10:04,660 --> 00:10:09,420
Smooth skin
in a jiffy!

158
00:10:04,710 --> 00:10:06,710
...with Spectaclean Body Wipes!

159
00:10:06,710 --> 00:10:09,420
Cut! That's perfect!

160
00:10:09,690 --> 00:10:11,630
Keep going!

161
00:10:11,970 --> 00:10:18,140
I offered you the ad 'cause a big sponsor 
has a <i>Tokyo Blade</i> fan for a daughter,

162
00:10:18,140 --> 00:10:19,600
and you two did great!

163
00:10:19,600 --> 00:10:21,380
I'm honored!

164
00:10:19,600 --> 00:10:21,380
I'm honored!

165
00:10:21,380 --> 00:10:24,690
Wow, you're in perfect sync. 
Your bad blood's all kayfabe, then?

166
00:10:26,570 --> 00:10:30,030
Haha! Of course it is!

167
00:10:26,570 --> 00:10:30,030
Haha! Of course it is!

168
00:10:30,030 --> 00:10:32,700
A rival? Who, her?

169
00:10:32,700 --> 00:10:34,780
Not a chance. 
She's nowhere near good enough.

170
00:10:34,780 --> 00:10:38,280
Wha? You got into it too, Kana-chan.

171
00:10:38,610 --> 00:10:40,540
Don't call me that!

172
00:10:43,430 --> 00:10:47,250
So, what'd you think? Did it help?

173
00:10:48,040 --> 00:10:50,650
You two really are amazing.

174
00:10:50,650 --> 00:10:53,220
You showed me how far I still have to go.

175
00:10:53,930 --> 00:10:56,040
How can I act like you?

176
00:10:58,110 --> 00:11:00,680
Know yourself.

177
00:11:01,000 --> 00:11:05,480
You need to have a good grasp 
of who you are on the inside.

178
00:11:06,170 --> 00:11:07,900
Who I am on the inside?

179
00:11:08,360 --> 00:11:13,200
For example, you take 
your likes and dislikes,

180
00:11:13,770 --> 00:11:17,110
and you either exaggerate 
or play them down as needed.

181
00:11:17,790 --> 00:11:18,630
Right.

182
00:11:18,930 --> 00:11:24,160
That way, you can form new rules 
and associations within your emotions.

183
00:11:25,180 --> 00:11:26,750
That's how you establish a characterâ€”

184
00:11:27,160 --> 00:11:29,400
the thing you're having 
trouble with right now.

185
00:11:29,400 --> 00:11:34,090
I place more emphasis on the 
character than myself, though.

186
00:11:34,090 --> 00:11:37,530
That much is obvious. 
You're a method actor.

187
00:11:40,410 --> 00:11:43,040
<i>Know myself?</i>

188
00:11:44,190 --> 00:11:46,840
<i>What kind of person </i>am<i> I?</i>

189
00:11:48,510 --> 00:11:50,770
<i>Am I Ruby?</i>

190
00:11:52,350 --> 00:11:55,540
<i>Am I Sarina Tendouji?</i>

191
00:11:57,110 --> 00:11:58,570
<i>Who am I?</i>

192
00:11:58,570 --> 00:12:00,820
Ichigo: Do you never think about meeting your mom?
Ai: Well, my mother hates me.
Ai: So I probably shouldn't. That's what's better for her, too.

193
00:12:02,320 --> 00:12:05,480
Mother doesn't love me.

194
00:12:06,690 --> 00:12:09,620
No. That can't be true.

195
00:12:10,190 --> 00:12:11,410
I mean...

196
00:12:17,970 --> 00:12:18,880
Mother!

197
00:12:19,630 --> 00:12:23,510
You came to see me! 
How long will you be staying?

198
00:12:24,170 --> 00:12:29,230
After I stop by your grandma's place, 
I have to head back to Tokyo.

199
00:12:31,170 --> 00:12:35,190
Oh. You must be busy with work.

200
00:12:35,500 --> 00:12:36,950
I'm sorry.

201
00:12:36,950 --> 00:12:39,610
I need to go speak to your doctor.

202
00:12:39,610 --> 00:12:42,370
Oh, okay...

203
00:12:47,680 --> 00:12:49,540
Hey, Mother?

204
00:12:53,810 --> 00:12:57,920
Do you love me?

205
00:12:58,950 --> 00:13:00,130
<i>I mean...</i>

206
00:13:01,840 --> 00:13:05,060
<i>There's no way those words were a lie.</i>

207
00:13:05,700 --> 00:13:08,270
Of course I love you.

208
00:13:15,980 --> 00:13:17,980
Tendouji

209
00:13:18,340 --> 00:13:21,990
<i>Many times, I found myself standing 
here when I was feeling down.</i>

210
00:13:22,690 --> 00:13:26,950
<i>My home still stood at the address 
I remembered it at.</i>

211
00:13:28,440 --> 00:13:32,170
<i>If I rang the bell, Mother would answer.</i>

212
00:13:33,630 --> 00:13:36,880
<i>So many times, I thought about 
pressing that button and saying...</i>

213
00:13:36,880 --> 00:13:41,340
Tendouji

214
00:13:38,390 --> 00:13:40,960
Mother, it's me.

215
00:13:42,610 --> 00:13:43,480
<i>But no.</i>

216
00:13:56,720 --> 00:14:02,400
Once upon a time, there was 
a perfectly ordinary family.

217
00:14:03,200 --> 00:14:06,620
As much affection as the mother 
showered the daughter with,

218
00:14:06,620 --> 00:14:10,870
she was found to have a serious 
illness when she was four.

219
00:14:11,730 --> 00:14:17,270
After learning her daughter had less than 
a 10% chance of living another 10 years,

220
00:14:17,270 --> 00:14:19,910
the mother treated her 
with love and care for a while,

221
00:14:19,910 --> 00:14:23,220
but in time, it broke her down mentally.

222
00:14:24,970 --> 00:14:31,310
The father separated the two and focused 
on helping the mother recover.

223
00:14:32,440 --> 00:14:36,230
They came from a respected family 
in the countryside,

224
00:14:36,230 --> 00:14:39,840
so they put the daughter in the care of 
the biggest hospital in their hometown.

225
00:14:40,990 --> 00:14:45,270
The parents threw themselves into work 
as if to run from their sorrows,

226
00:14:45,270 --> 00:14:48,020
and soon they would refuse 
to see reality for what it was.

227
00:14:49,500 --> 00:14:53,880
Eventually, they started to avert 
their eyes from their daughter, too.

228
00:14:54,780 --> 00:14:57,350
My mother used to be a figure skater!

229
00:14:57,350 --> 00:15:01,460
She says she'll teach me how 
to skate once I'm discharged!

230
00:15:01,940 --> 00:15:06,930
I want to make the Olympics 
and put a smile on her face!

231
00:15:07,790 --> 00:15:11,640
The daughter's condition 
only grew worse with time.

232
00:15:12,300 --> 00:15:14,940
She battled chronic headaches and nausea,

233
00:15:15,570 --> 00:15:19,540
and she lost her sense of balance, 
which left her unable to walk.

234
00:15:21,630 --> 00:15:25,030
It affected her memory 
and situational awareness, too.

235
00:15:26,340 --> 00:15:30,240
During those days of suffering, 
she found solace in one special girl.

236
00:15:32,260 --> 00:15:36,410
The daughter came to live 
vicariously through her.

237
00:15:37,550 --> 00:15:43,680
As her condition became terminal, 
the mother stopped showing up at all.

238
00:15:44,520 --> 00:15:47,850
She must not have wanted 
to see her daughter in pain.

239
00:15:49,050 --> 00:15:54,160
But the girl continued 
to wait for her mother.

240
00:15:56,230 --> 00:16:01,310
She continued to wait for her mother, 
believing that she still loved her.

241
00:16:06,260 --> 00:16:08,820
Oh, it's just you, Sensei.

242
00:16:08,820 --> 00:16:11,160
Too bad it's just me.

243
00:16:13,060 --> 00:16:15,200
Hmm? That's, uh, B-Komachi?

244
00:16:15,830 --> 00:16:17,430
They released a new single?

245
00:16:17,430 --> 00:16:18,160
Yep!

246
00:16:18,880 --> 00:16:24,220
The young man had a habit of going to see 
patients who didn't get visitors

247
00:16:24,220 --> 00:16:26,280
and making small talk with them.

248
00:16:27,190 --> 00:16:31,720
It's impossible to quantify just 
how much that helped the daughter.

249
00:16:32,750 --> 00:16:36,100
She had found two rays of hope.

250
00:16:37,200 --> 00:16:43,060
Though she would come 
to lose them both in time.

251
00:16:38,100 --> 00:16:43,570
Ai's Fan for All Eternity!!!

252
00:16:45,750 --> 00:16:50,820
Even as she spent most of her 
short life in a small room,

253
00:16:51,320 --> 00:16:52,960
fought through the pain,

254
00:16:53,410 --> 00:16:55,370
B-Komachi

255
00:16:53,800 --> 00:16:55,370
and had her dreams shattered,

256
00:16:56,070 --> 00:17:00,590
she still continued to wait for 
her mother, day after day.

257
00:17:01,570 --> 00:17:03,790
She continued to believe 
that she was loved.

258
00:17:04,830 --> 00:17:06,500
But even on the day it all ended,

259
00:17:07,370 --> 00:17:10,030
in her final hours,

260
00:17:10,030 --> 00:17:13,340
the mother did not appear before her.

261
00:17:15,920 --> 00:17:19,920
As she heard the news in silence 
in their Tokyo home,

262
00:17:21,200 --> 00:17:24,730
what must've gone through 
the mother's mind?

263
00:17:26,190 --> 00:17:29,000
As a mother who ran 
and ran from her daughter,

264
00:17:29,410 --> 00:17:32,910
what exactly did she even mean to her?

265
00:17:34,820 --> 00:17:37,240
Soon after the girl died,

266
00:17:37,990 --> 00:17:40,670
the mother gave birth 
to a son and daughter.

267
00:17:43,210 --> 00:17:45,800
And now, they all live happily ever after.

268
00:17:47,880 --> 00:17:50,000
All's well that ends well.

269
00:17:56,650 --> 00:18:01,520
I've never seen Mother 
smile like that before.

270
00:18:02,710 --> 00:18:06,560
I knew it. I knew it somewhere deep down.

271
00:18:07,720 --> 00:18:10,440
I wanted her to love me.

272
00:18:10,950 --> 00:18:15,030
But she didn't love me!

273
00:18:16,080 --> 00:18:19,520
That's why I saw Mom as a replacement.

274
00:18:19,520 --> 00:18:22,250
I pushed my disgusting wishes onto her.

275
00:18:22,890 --> 00:18:24,960
What the hell am I?!

276
00:18:24,960 --> 00:18:28,420
Everyone in my life ends up suffering!

277
00:18:28,910 --> 00:18:31,170
All I bring is misfortune!

278
00:18:31,860 --> 00:18:35,800
To Mother, Mom, and Sensei...

279
00:18:36,580 --> 00:18:41,800
Tell me, gods. Why did you 
reincarnate a plague like me?

280
00:18:43,370 --> 00:18:46,770
Sensei, have you ever been to, 
like, Shibuya or Harajuku?

281
00:18:47,060 --> 00:18:49,920
Yeah. I did go to college in Tokyo.

282
00:18:49,920 --> 00:18:51,860
That's so cool!

283
00:18:52,110 --> 00:18:54,570
Those places are full of life, right?

284
00:18:55,030 --> 00:18:58,910
Filled with lots of people, 
and even talent scouts.

285
00:18:59,510 --> 00:19:02,740
Ai said she got scouted in Shibuya, too!

286
00:19:02,740 --> 00:19:03,620
Yeah?

287
00:19:04,200 --> 00:19:07,020
I'll show you around the place 
when you're better.

288
00:19:07,020 --> 00:19:07,830
Really?!

289
00:19:08,410 --> 00:19:10,040
You're really cute,

290
00:19:10,040 --> 00:19:12,540
so I'm sure you'll get 
approached by scouts.

291
00:19:13,010 --> 00:19:17,520
But I'll send scouts from underground idol
groups and other shady places packing.

292
00:19:17,520 --> 00:19:21,220
But I'd love to be an idol, 
underground or not.

293
00:19:21,620 --> 00:19:24,020
I want to be like Ai 
and wear stylish outfits,

294
00:19:24,020 --> 00:19:27,650
sing cute songs, 
have the crowds do calls for me,

295
00:19:28,020 --> 00:19:29,730
take the stage in huge venues,

296
00:19:29,730 --> 00:19:32,260
and put smiles on lots of people's faces!

297
00:19:33,180 --> 00:19:34,500
That's so dreamy!

298
00:19:34,500 --> 00:19:36,030
Not a chance.

299
00:19:36,560 --> 00:19:39,140
Show business is a scary place.

300
00:19:39,140 --> 00:19:43,180
I won't allow it unless you have a good 
agency repping and looking out for you.

301
00:19:43,180 --> 00:19:45,370
Jeez, you're too overprotective!

302
00:19:54,200 --> 00:19:56,670
Why did I even become an idol?!

303
00:19:58,550 --> 00:19:59,640
Take it easy.

304
00:20:00,040 --> 00:20:01,690
Take a deep, long breath.

305
00:20:02,590 --> 00:20:05,310
You need to lie down. Can you stand?

306
00:20:06,470 --> 00:20:07,670
The script...

307
00:20:08,130 --> 00:20:09,410
Where's my script?

308
00:20:10,470 --> 00:20:12,160
I need to rehearse.

309
00:20:12,160 --> 00:20:13,730
You're in no state for that.

310
00:20:14,230 --> 00:20:15,640
Come on, grab on to me.

311
00:20:15,640 --> 00:20:17,450
I don't want your help, Aqua!

312
00:20:19,470 --> 00:20:23,240
That's right. The reason I'm an idol

313
00:20:24,370 --> 00:20:29,710
is so I can make it to the top and find 
the guy who killed Mom and Sensei.

314
00:20:30,120 --> 00:20:32,670
To avenge Mom and Sensei!

315
00:20:33,200 --> 00:20:35,720
I'll find him if it's the last thing I do.

316
00:20:35,720 --> 00:20:38,860
And I'll make him regret 
ever coming into this world!

317
00:20:40,980 --> 00:20:42,050
Stop that.

318
00:20:42,620 --> 00:20:47,430
Living for revenge will bring you 
nothing but pain and suffering.

319
00:20:47,990 --> 00:20:50,940
There's no need for you to do that.

320
00:20:51,960 --> 00:20:52,690
Please.

321
00:20:53,850 --> 00:20:56,830
Forget about revenge 
and live your own life.

322
00:20:57,530 --> 00:20:59,400
Don't tell me what to do.

323
00:21:00,010 --> 00:21:02,640
Quit trying to act like my big bro now.

324
00:21:02,640 --> 00:21:06,740
I don't see you as real family.

325
00:21:07,370 --> 00:21:12,640
We're total strangers. We just happened 
to be reborn in the same place.

326
00:21:14,590 --> 00:21:17,460
Fine. You're free to think that.

327
00:21:18,820 --> 00:21:21,920
I'm not about to call us 
brother and sister now.

328
00:21:22,410 --> 00:21:24,680
I know I have no right to.

329
00:21:25,430 --> 00:21:27,640
And I'm fully aware 
that I'm being a hypocrite.

330
00:21:28,450 --> 00:21:29,520
But...

331
00:21:29,830 --> 00:21:32,520
I'm not asking as Aqua Hoshino.

332
00:21:32,990 --> 00:21:34,730
Please listen to <i>me,</i>

333
00:21:35,220 --> 00:21:36,420
Sarina-chan.

334
00:21:38,000 --> 00:21:41,200
I know this isn't why 
you wanted to be an idol.

335
00:21:42,180 --> 00:21:43,910
You got out of that hospital room.

336
00:21:44,290 --> 00:21:46,700
You're finally free to live 
the life you want.

337
00:21:47,950 --> 00:21:50,600
Didn't you want to be like Ai 
and wear stylish outfits,

338
00:21:50,600 --> 00:21:53,980
sing cute songs, 
have the crowds do calls for you,

339
00:21:53,980 --> 00:21:57,120
take the stage in huge venues, 
and put smiles on lots of people's faces?!

340
00:21:58,030 --> 00:22:01,520
Didn't you become an idol 
to make those dreams come true?!

341
00:22:02,490 --> 00:22:07,390
<i>A singular thought, "What if?" 
has crossed my mind time and time again.</i>

342
00:22:08,720 --> 00:22:11,600
<i>Every time I felt I saw 
traces of Sarina-chan in you,</i>

343
00:22:11,600 --> 00:22:13,400
<i>I turned around and beat myself up.</i>

344
00:22:14,310 --> 00:22:18,210
<i>I hated myself for ever having 
such self-serving fantasies.</i>

345
00:22:19,560 --> 00:22:22,500
<i>After being powerless 
to do anything to help Sarina-chan,</i>

346
00:22:22,500 --> 00:22:24,860
<i>there was no way I'd ever 
get a second chance.</i>

347
00:22:25,580 --> 00:22:28,240
<i>But all these years,</i>

348
00:22:28,790 --> 00:22:31,490
<i>I've treated you just like 
I would have treated her.</i>

349
00:22:32,430 --> 00:22:35,080
Forget about revenge.

350
00:22:36,140 --> 00:22:37,970
I'm begging you, Ruby.

351
00:22:39,310 --> 00:22:40,350
Why?

352
00:22:41,530 --> 00:22:43,150
Why are you crying?

353
00:22:44,340 --> 00:22:48,080
Why did you just call me Sarina?

354
00:22:49,700 --> 00:22:53,230
How do you know 
about that time in the hospital?

355
00:22:54,670 --> 00:22:55,690
Tell me...

356
00:22:56,780 --> 00:22:59,240
Could it be...?

357
00:23:01,140 --> 00:23:03,980
Are you Sensei?

358
00:23:08,870 --> 00:23:11,720
I've been looking for this.

359
00:23:13,240 --> 00:23:15,290
You held onto it for me, huh,

360
00:23:16,350 --> 00:23:17,670
Sarina-chan?

361
00:24:08,600 --> 00:24:11,420
Sensei!

362
00:24:11,760 --> 00:24:15,450
You've always been this close?

363
00:24:15,450 --> 00:24:16,390
Why?

364
00:24:16,730 --> 00:24:18,850
Why did you never tell me?

365
00:24:19,630 --> 00:24:23,140
Uh, I wasn't sure until just now.

366
00:24:23,140 --> 00:24:24,730
You dummy!

367
00:24:24,730 --> 00:24:26,930
I worked so hard!

368
00:24:26,930 --> 00:24:32,330
I thought you'd find me if 
I called myself a B-Komachi idol.

369
00:24:32,710 --> 00:24:37,290
I always looked for you 
among the crowd at every event.

370
00:24:37,290 --> 00:24:40,290
I thought you might be 
somewhere out there watching,

371
00:24:40,290 --> 00:24:43,130
so I gave my all each time!

372
00:24:43,880 --> 00:24:47,940
I was worried you'd forgotten 
all about Mom and B-Komachi,

373
00:24:48,420 --> 00:24:51,240
and that maybe you'd never find me.

374
00:24:52,390 --> 00:24:56,780
I called the hospital and 
they said you were missing.

375
00:24:56,780 --> 00:24:58,230
And then what?

376
00:24:58,830 --> 00:25:01,190
I find you dead in a cave?

377
00:25:01,560 --> 00:25:04,270
I'm sorry. I put you through a lot.

378
00:25:04,920 --> 00:25:10,360
I trusted you, Aqua, but then 
you went and sold Mom out.

379
00:25:10,910 --> 00:25:15,660
It made me feel like I couldn't 
trust anybody in the world.

380
00:25:15,660 --> 00:25:17,280
I didn't forget.

381
00:25:18,150 --> 00:25:23,250
I told the world about Ai's secret and 
spurred the director to make this movie

382
00:25:24,080 --> 00:25:26,750
all to get revenge for Ai.

383
00:25:28,590 --> 00:25:32,890
I thought I had to avenge Mom and you,

384
00:25:32,890 --> 00:25:35,890
Dig Deep!
Chase the Impawsible!!

385
00:25:32,890 --> 00:25:35,890
Dig Deep!
Chase the Impawsible!!

386
00:25:32,890 --> 00:25:35,890
Special Episode Pitch

387
00:25:33,680 --> 00:25:35,890
so I did lots of awful things.

388
00:25:36,510 --> 00:25:38,950
I told lots of lies.

389
00:25:39,310 --> 00:25:42,610
Every time I did, 
a pain shot through my chest,

390
00:25:42,610 --> 00:25:45,520
and I felt a knot in my stomach.

391
00:25:46,350 --> 00:25:52,520
The more I lied, the more I felt I was 
drifting away from what I wanted to be.

392
00:25:52,950 --> 00:25:56,510
Ruby, that stuff is not you.

393
00:25:57,520 --> 00:25:58,410
But...

394
00:25:58,820 --> 00:26:02,110
Mom always said idols 
were made up of lies.

395
00:26:02,110 --> 00:26:04,830
You and Ai are different people.

396
00:26:06,750 --> 00:26:09,090
Stop chasing after her shadow.

397
00:26:09,650 --> 00:26:11,920
Live your own life.

398
00:26:12,930 --> 00:26:14,390
You don't have to lie about anything.

399
00:26:16,810 --> 00:26:19,120
You know, the truth is...

400
00:26:19,770 --> 00:26:21,090
It hurt.

401
00:26:21,660 --> 00:26:27,540
I thought I had to tell believable lies 
and be all smiles all the time like Mom.

402
00:26:28,030 --> 00:26:30,220
I thought I had to be like her.

403
00:26:31,590 --> 00:26:36,180
Being an idol wasn't 
all rainbows and sunshine at all.

404
00:26:36,180 --> 00:26:40,490
So many times, I thought it'd be so much 
easier if I could just forget about her.

405
00:26:42,100 --> 00:26:46,750
When I looked at the fans, sometimes 
I'd think back to her killer's face.

406
00:26:46,750 --> 00:26:53,250
I had all these nasty, 
disgusting thoughts,

407
00:26:54,150 --> 00:26:58,800
but I hid them all because 
I wanted to be loved.

408
00:26:59,610 --> 00:27:04,390
I hadn't changed at all from the time 
I spent hating the world in the hospital.

409
00:27:05,570 --> 00:27:07,690
How can that be good enough?

410
00:27:07,690 --> 00:27:10,190
Am I really good enough like that?

411
00:27:11,400 --> 00:27:14,600
I told you I'd be your 
number one fan, remember?

412
00:27:15,550 --> 00:27:17,070
I said that because,

413
00:27:17,690 --> 00:27:20,530
even as you suffered in pain 
in that hospital room,

414
00:27:20,910 --> 00:27:25,280
you still looked straight ahead with 
stars in your eyes and continued to dream.

415
00:27:26,130 --> 00:27:29,920
Back then, you shone far brighter 
than Ai ever did!

416
00:27:34,730 --> 00:27:36,130
Good for you.

417
00:27:36,130 --> 00:27:38,580
Now Ruby will bounce back,

418
00:27:38,580 --> 00:27:41,970
and you'll get to make your movie 
just like you wanted.

419
00:27:42,320 --> 00:27:46,440
This might just inspire her 
to even greater heights.

420
00:27:47,060 --> 00:27:51,390
If so, that would make me very happy, too.

421
00:27:53,310 --> 00:27:54,030
But...

422
00:27:54,690 --> 00:27:57,520
Are you really sure about this?

423
00:27:58,280 --> 00:28:02,780
It might've been easier for you 
if she'd continued to hate you.

424
00:28:08,780 --> 00:28:10,840
<i>I'll trust you, Onii-chan.</i>

425
00:28:11,720 --> 00:28:16,820
<i>I'll trust that the girl you said you'd be 
a fan of can shine brighter than Mom.</i>

426
00:28:18,950 --> 00:28:20,010
<i>Also...</i>

427
00:28:20,340 --> 00:28:23,010
<i>I haven't forgotten those words.</i>

428
00:28:24,310 --> 00:28:28,960
<i>You said you'd marry me once 
I turned sixteen, remember?</i>

429
00:28:31,410 --> 00:28:36,120
Sensei? I'm sixteen now.

430
00:28:39,650 --> 00:28:41,700
I'm wiped!

431
00:28:42,110 --> 00:28:44,160
Onii-chan, gimme some of your juice.

432
00:28:44,440 --> 00:28:46,260
No. Get your own.

433
00:28:47,810 --> 00:28:51,380
Too late. You snooze, you lose juice.

434
00:28:51,730 --> 00:28:54,130
Ah, I'm coming back to life!

435
00:28:54,130 --> 00:28:55,020
Get off of me.

436
00:28:55,020 --> 00:28:56,290
You're damp with sweat.

437
00:28:56,290 --> 00:28:59,490
Hey, let me have this.

438
00:28:59,490 --> 00:29:01,040
What the hell happened?!

439
00:29:01,040 --> 00:29:04,640
Whoa, you startled me. 
Why'd you start yelling out of nowhere?

440
00:29:04,640 --> 00:29:06,600
We're the ones startled here!

441
00:29:06,920 --> 00:29:08,220
Ever heard of personal space?

442
00:29:08,580 --> 00:29:10,230
You two are stuck together like glue!

443
00:29:10,500 --> 00:29:14,540
Oh, you know how Onii-chan 
and I had been fighting lately?

444
00:29:14,540 --> 00:29:17,190
Well, we made up the other day,

445
00:29:18,400 --> 00:29:20,180
and now we're making up for lost time.

446
00:29:20,180 --> 00:29:21,740
More like <i>over</i>compensating!

447
00:29:21,740 --> 00:29:26,770
You're part of the problem, Aqua! 
Tell your sister off!

448
00:29:26,770 --> 00:29:29,470
I <i>could</i> do that, or I could just 
let her do whatever she wants.

449
00:29:29,470 --> 00:29:31,750
Right. I forgot he was 
obsessed with his sister.

450
00:29:31,750 --> 00:29:33,960
We've always been thick as thieves!

451
00:29:35,190 --> 00:29:36,800
Get off of him already!

452
00:29:36,800 --> 00:29:38,340
Hold it!

453
00:29:38,650 --> 00:29:41,220
They're two hot twins 
that look hot together!

454
00:29:41,220 --> 00:29:43,720
Lemme take pics for Insta!

455
00:29:44,930 --> 00:29:47,640
Ugh, you engagement junkie.

456
00:29:50,380 --> 00:29:52,440
I can't. That was so friggin' weird.

457
00:29:52,880 --> 00:29:55,080
I could smell the degeneracy in the air.

458
00:29:56,810 --> 00:30:00,450
Well, Ruby's got a lot on her plate.

459
00:30:00,450 --> 00:30:04,020
I bet she just wanted somebody to lean on.

460
00:30:04,660 --> 00:30:07,080
She's using him as a crutch, basically.

461
00:30:07,920 --> 00:30:11,540
If it's only as bad as needing an 
emotional support, that's fine.

462
00:30:11,540 --> 00:30:16,300
But the only way to really fix it is to do 
something about her packed schedule.

463
00:30:16,750 --> 00:30:18,710
The 15-Year Lie

464
00:30:16,750 --> 00:30:20,030
Heck, she's actually 
hit a wall with her acting.

465
00:30:20,030 --> 00:30:22,220
She desperately needs more rehearsal time.

466
00:30:22,870 --> 00:30:25,180
I'm glad she seems to be feeling better,

467
00:30:25,180 --> 00:30:28,380
but motivation and high spirits won't be 
enough to get her through this movie.

468
00:30:30,300 --> 00:30:36,150
If anything, she's at even more risk 
now with this mental doping.

469
00:30:36,150 --> 00:30:39,050
If she goes too hard and breaks down, 
it'll have all been for naught.

470
00:30:39,050 --> 00:30:40,400
Right you are.

471
00:30:41,030 --> 00:30:44,490
But this is Ruby's best chance 
to make a move at superstardom.

472
00:30:45,120 --> 00:30:51,240
Sure, she has to juggle TV appearances, 
events, concerts, and acting lessons...

473
00:30:51,240 --> 00:30:52,690
And her studies, too.

474
00:30:52,690 --> 00:30:53,710
Studies!

475
00:30:53,710 --> 00:30:56,140
Right, those exist!

476
00:30:56,140 --> 00:30:58,920
Mine were so long ago that 
I forgot all about the concept!

477
00:30:58,920 --> 00:31:02,420
I'm amazed you managed to keep up 
your high school girl gimmick like that.

478
00:31:02,920 --> 00:31:05,830
Either way, it'll be hard 
to strike the right balance.

479
00:31:05,830 --> 00:31:09,640
All we can do is hope 
the president takes care of it.

480
00:31:10,310 --> 00:31:13,810
Even if Strawberry Pro 
has experienced this before with Ai,

481
00:31:13,810 --> 00:31:16,600
it was the previous president 
at the helm at the time.

482
00:31:17,140 --> 00:31:21,360
This is probably a real test of 
President Miyako's ability, as well.

483
00:31:22,110 --> 00:31:25,100
Right. We're very grateful.

484
00:31:25,100 --> 00:31:29,650
I'll take a good look at Ruby's 
schedule and get back to you.

485
00:31:35,680 --> 00:31:41,070
Covering a charity event for 
28-Hour TV? That's a huge gig.

486
00:31:49,220 --> 00:31:51,840
<i>I can make room in her schedule.</i>

487
00:31:52,250 --> 00:31:55,850
<i>But do I really want to give 
Ruby even more work?</i>

488
00:31:56,730 --> 00:31:59,020
Reduce the amount of work she takes on.

489
00:31:59,840 --> 00:32:03,560
Especially for the duration 
of filming and rehearsals.

490
00:32:06,860 --> 00:32:09,080
<i>There's so much to think about.</i>

491
00:32:13,700 --> 00:32:18,460
Keep this marketing rep named Tendouji 
as far away from Ruby as possible.

492
00:32:19,020 --> 00:32:20,210
Did something happen?

493
00:32:21,160 --> 00:32:24,410
