I finally found you.

556
00:36:10,040 --> 00:36:11,770
M-Miyako...

557
00:36:12,150 --> 00:36:13,480
Calm down a seâ€”

558
00:36:14,170 --> 00:36:20,450
Do you have any goddamn idea 
how I've felt all these years?

559
00:36:21,550 --> 00:36:27,680
You abandoned the promise you made me 
to run off and do what, you asshole?!

560
00:36:35,340 --> 00:36:37,300
[Express] Shinjuku Station

561
00:36:42,880 --> 00:36:47,810
<i>The first time I saw Tokyo, it was covered 
in bright lights from top to bottom.</i>

562
00:36:48,130 --> 00:36:51,080
<i>It instantly stole my heart away.</i>

563
00:36:54,030 --> 00:36:58,030
<i>I felt that this city was where 
I was meant to live my life.</i>

564
00:36:59,470 --> 00:37:01,820
<i>The nightlife was like a video game.</i>

565
00:37:03,450 --> 00:37:07,330
<i>I took out the fodder, 
built up XP and gold,</i>

566
00:37:07,750 --> 00:37:09,540
<i>leveled up,</i>

567
00:37:09,950 --> 00:37:12,000
<i>bought more powerful weapons,</i>

568
00:37:13,750 --> 00:37:18,870
<i>spent increasingly more time 
around stupidly loaded people,</i>

569
00:37:18,870 --> 00:37:21,800
<i>started seeing the guys in college 
as snot-nosed brats,</i>

570
00:37:22,220 --> 00:37:29,350
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100

571
00:37:22,220 --> 00:37:23,640
A wild Self-Proclaimed Tech CEO appeared!
A wild Self-Proclaimed Investor appeared!

572
00:37:22,890 --> 00:37:27,440
<i>defeated stronger foes, 
built up lots more XP,</i>

573
00:37:23,720 --> 00:37:25,100
Miyako used Blow Kiss!

574
00:37:25,140 --> 00:37:26,390
The Self-Proclaimed Tech CEO was defeated!
The Self-Proclaimed Investor was defeated!

575
00:37:26,470 --> 00:37:27,930
Miyako leveled up!

576
00:37:27,440 --> 00:37:29,350
<i>leveled up even more,</i>

577
00:37:28,020 --> 00:37:29,350
Miyako evolved from
cabaret club girl to lounge girl!

578
00:37:29,350 --> 00:37:32,850
Cabaret Club

579
00:37:29,660 --> 00:37:32,000
<i>switched classes, and grew stronger.</i>

580
00:37:30,730 --> 00:37:32,850
Lounge

581
00:37:32,060 --> 00:37:32,850
Hostess Club

582
00:37:33,220 --> 00:37:36,570
<i>Tokyo's good to strong people like that,</i>

583
00:37:36,570 --> 00:37:39,570
<i>and it affirmed my way of life.</i>

584
00:37:40,490 --> 00:37:45,080
<i>I played the game smart and 
followed this city's unspoken rules,</i>

585
00:37:46,400 --> 00:37:50,800
<i>and I was sure I'd keep 
climbing to ever greater heights.</i>

586
00:37:54,670 --> 00:37:56,380
The hottest, "biggest" new face

587
00:37:54,670 --> 00:37:56,380
Dynamite College Girl!!

588
00:37:58,340 --> 00:38:01,830
<i>But it would all come crashing to an end.</i>

589
00:38:03,310 --> 00:38:05,860
<i>Tokyo was full of attractive girls,</i>

590
00:38:05,860 --> 00:38:10,060
<i>and I didn't have that special 
something to make it in showbiz.</i>

591
00:38:11,740 --> 00:38:16,060
<i>I got more chances to interact with 
big shots due to being an entertainer,</i>

592
00:38:16,730 --> 00:38:18,600
<i>but that didn't last long either.</i>

593
00:38:19,190 --> 00:38:21,650
Checking Inbox

594
00:38:19,190 --> 00:38:20,320
Checking...

595
00:38:19,480 --> 00:38:21,650
<i>By the time I graduated college,</i>

596
00:38:20,320 --> 00:38:21,650
No New Mail

597
00:38:21,920 --> 00:38:25,490
<i>I'd stopped getting invited 
to parties by business owners.</i>

598
00:38:26,990 --> 00:38:29,090
<i>Not that I cared.</i>

599
00:38:29,090 --> 00:38:31,230
<i>Those guys cheated at the drop of a hat.</i>

600
00:38:31,230 --> 00:38:33,710
<i>I would've never found happiness 
in life going out with them.</i>

601
00:38:34,630 --> 00:38:37,340
<i>A Minato-ku trophy girl 
who was no longer in demand</i>

602
00:38:37,340 --> 00:38:42,260
<i>could only stick around by becoming an 
intermediary who summoned younger girls.</i>

603
00:38:43,630 --> 00:38:46,040
<i>And I hung on pathetically 
by doing just that.</i>

604
00:38:47,920 --> 00:38:50,890
<i>More and more men started 
asking me to be their mistress.</i>

605
00:38:52,130 --> 00:38:57,540
<i>Those scumbags are very good at sniffing 
out women at risk of losing their spot,</i>

606
00:38:57,540 --> 00:38:59,900
<i>and they try to exploit them 
for all they're worth.</i>

607
00:39:01,060 --> 00:39:05,700
<i>They use the starry-eyed girls 
until they get tired of them.</i>

608
00:39:05,700 --> 00:39:07,370
Hup.

609
00:39:08,610 --> 00:39:09,390
Heya.

610
00:39:18,870 --> 00:39:23,460
Listen, are you gonna keep 
working the night life forever?

611
00:39:34,930 --> 00:39:38,080
If you don't have a goal in mind, 
wanna come work for me?

612
00:39:49,700 --> 00:39:56,290
<i>I was a girl who longed for the bright 
lights but couldn't cut it in showbiz.</i>

613
00:39:54,080 --> 00:39:56,290
Strawberry Productions

614
00:39:56,660 --> 00:40:01,840
<i>How ironic was it that I'd now be working 
to help others pursue their dreams?</i>

615
00:40:03,080 --> 00:40:03,670
<i>But...</i>

616
00:40:04,550 --> 00:40:08,920
<i>Seeing the lights from backstage 
didn't feel as bad as I'd thought.</i>

617
00:40:12,650 --> 00:40:13,720
Miyako.

618
00:40:15,400 --> 00:40:17,770
Will you stay by my side and support me?

619
00:40:18,990 --> 00:40:20,980
I'll work my butt off.

620
00:40:21,840 --> 00:40:24,090
And if you'll be my pillarâ€”my wifeâ€”

621
00:40:24,550 --> 00:40:27,450
I'll show you the most 
dazzling sight in the world.

622
00:40:28,330 --> 00:40:30,800
The most dazzling sight...?

623
00:40:32,420 --> 00:40:34,370
Wow!

624
00:40:34,810 --> 00:40:38,040
I bet it'd feel so good 
if we performed here.

625
00:40:38,670 --> 00:40:42,170
You mean <i>when</i> we perform here.

626
00:40:42,170 --> 00:40:43,160
Right.

627
00:40:43,160 --> 00:40:45,060
It's so huge.

628
00:40:45,060 --> 00:40:46,590
Sure is.

629
00:40:46,590 --> 00:40:48,940
Do you actually think that?

630
00:40:48,940 --> 00:40:50,340
I do, I do.

631
00:40:50,340 --> 00:40:52,230
Really, now?

632
00:40:52,230 --> 00:40:53,800
Really! I mean it!

633
00:40:53,800 --> 00:40:57,810
One day, we'll light up 
Tokyo Dome with glow sticks.

634
00:40:58,450 --> 00:41:00,020
That's our dream.

635
00:41:15,660 --> 00:41:18,210
You said you'd show me!

636
00:41:19,820 --> 00:41:24,250
How could you just throw in the towel 
and run away from it all?!

637
00:41:27,630 --> 00:41:32,300
When I... I still haven't given up on it!

638
00:41:36,310 --> 00:41:40,790
You said it was our dream!

639
00:41:51,010 --> 00:41:55,950
So, Strawberry Productions will undergo 
a major organizational restructuring.

640
00:41:56,240 --> 00:41:58,660
Before that, 
I guess I should introduce you.

641
00:42:01,870 --> 00:42:04,230
That's Ichigo Saitou-kun, 
our new errand boy.

642
00:42:04,740 --> 00:42:06,220
Hello, I'm Saitou.

643
00:42:07,710 --> 00:42:10,860
First, for your new assignments...

644
00:42:10,860 --> 00:42:13,050
Take a look at the handout.

645
00:42:13,430 --> 00:42:15,510
Hayashi will handle 
the cross-media talent.

646
00:42:16,010 --> 00:42:18,600
Streamer Group A goes to Sasami,

647
00:42:18,950 --> 00:42:20,810
and Group B to Terabayashi.

648
00:42:21,230 --> 00:42:24,460
Yoshizumi will manage 
MEM and Arima of B-Komachi.

649
00:42:25,030 --> 00:42:29,280
And I'll take over 
as Ruby and Aqua's manager.

650
00:42:30,030 --> 00:42:31,870
Everything else remains the same.

651
00:42:31,870 --> 00:42:32,820
Huh?

652
00:42:32,820 --> 00:42:36,020
But then, who runs the agency?

653
00:42:36,020 --> 00:42:37,520
Beats me.

654
00:42:38,290 --> 00:42:41,100
Maybe that errand boy over there 
will take care of it.

655
00:42:43,470 --> 00:42:45,110
Who is that?

656
00:42:45,110 --> 00:42:48,270
The president's husband. 
The one who founded this agency.

657
00:42:48,270 --> 00:42:49,050
What?!

658
00:42:50,510 --> 00:42:52,960
That's all from me. Back to work.

659
00:42:59,040 --> 00:43:01,820
Good for you! You got to talk 
things out with Miyako-san!

660
00:43:01,820 --> 00:43:05,020
I can't believe you can say that 
after seeing this face.

661
00:43:05,020 --> 00:43:07,580
I was half coerced into it.

662
00:43:07,580 --> 00:43:09,340
She threatened to sue me,

663
00:43:09,340 --> 00:43:11,650
and when I tried to argue, 
she literally threw hands.

664
00:43:12,100 --> 00:43:14,280
But you came back anyway.

665
00:43:14,840 --> 00:43:17,410
I'm happy for you. 
You wanted to all along, didn't you?

666
00:43:22,480 --> 00:43:26,420
You got me so much work, even 
though you weren't an agent here.

667
00:43:26,930 --> 00:43:30,000
Easier to do that when you're 
officially part of the agency, right?

668
00:43:31,550 --> 00:43:34,760
That's not it. I was set up.

669
00:43:36,000 --> 00:43:37,090
By whom?

670
00:43:37,420 --> 00:43:39,380
Aqua, who else?

671
00:43:39,600 --> 00:43:42,350
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100

672
00:43:39,600 --> 00:43:42,350
< Aqua Hoshino

673
00:43:39,600 --> 00:43:42,350
We need to talk about Ruby

674
00:43:39,600 --> 00:43:42,350
Can you come to Samidare
at 2 AM tonight?

675
00:43:39,600 --> 00:43:42,350
Talk about sudden

676
